ower)            \/\/ [10, 20]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [30, 40, 50]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The elements are a random-access collection in ascending order, indexed by rank like an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array: ","type":"text"},{"code":"tree[0]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the smallest element. The vertices live in flat arrays with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int32","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"links, so the tree holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1 elements, and copying it copies a few arrays only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when one copy is mutated.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees\/splaytree"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://BinarySearchTrees/ST":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sequence","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/ST"},"doc://BinarySearchTrees/documentation/BinarySearchTrees/Treap":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Treap","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Treap","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees\/treap","kind":"symbol","title":"Treap","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A sorted set kept in a treap: a binary search tree whose vertices also carry random"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"priorities, with no vertex of higher priority than its parent (Seidel and Aragon, 1996)."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://BinarySearchTrees/s8SendableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8SendableP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable"},"doc://BinarySearchTrees/documentation/BinarySearchTrees/SplayTree/subscript(checked:)":{"